1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,120
Imagine your recipe

2
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:02,480
website yesterday.

3
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:03,360
A title,

4
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,080
a menu,

5
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:05,120
and a photo.

6
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,560
Today you change

7
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:07,440
the title.

8
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:07,920
When you

9
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,200
record that change,

10
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:09,680
what does

11
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,680
Git remember?

12
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:12,420
A snapshot records

13
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:12,980
the project

14
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:13,540
state at

15
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:14,020
one point

16
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:14,820
in history.

17
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:15,460
A commit

18
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:15,940
points to

19
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:16,980
that snapshot,

20
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,020
the tracked file

21
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:18,820
versions chosen

22
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:19,860
for that commit,

23
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:20,980
including content that

24
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:21,980
stayed the same.

25
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:22,760
So the

26
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,040
next snapshot describes

27
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:24,440
the new

28
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:24,920
title,

29
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:25,320
the same

30
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:25,800
menu,

31
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:26,120
and the

32
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,000
same photo.

33
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:27,320
It is

34
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,360
a complete recorded

35
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:28,760
state,

36
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,240
rather than

37
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:29,560
just an

38
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,320
edit list.

39
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:31,260
This is

40
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,540
a logical snapshot,

41
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:32,780
not a

42
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:33,580
screenshot or

43
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:33,980
a fresh

44
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:34,380
copy of

45
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:35,580
your entire disk.

46
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:36,700
Git can reuse

47
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,460
unchanged content internally.

48
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,060
Untracked files are outside

49
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,220
that recorded state.

50
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,560
Changes tell

51
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,680
you what differs.

52
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,120
A snapshot records

53
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:45,880
what was there.
